             <p>All data processing occurs locally on your device:</p>
             <p><strong>Biometric Data:</strong> Heart rate variability (HRV), heart rate, and breathing patterns from Apple Watch or HealthKit are processed in real-time on your device to influence audio, visuals, and lighting. Individual readings are not stored, and none of this is transmitted by the app.</p>
             <p><strong>Your performer signature:</strong> So that the same preset does not compose the same-sounding piece for everyone, Echoelmusic keeps one small summary on your device — coarse averages of your resting heart rate, variability, breathing rate and coherence, learned slowly while you play. It is used for a single purpose: to seed the music generator, so what the instrument creates carries your musical handwriting. It is never shown as a health reading, never used for advertising, never compared with other users, and never transmitted. It is stored in the app's own preferences, so it is included in an iCloud or encrypted local device backup of your phone. <strong>You can erase it at any time:</strong> open <em>Save &amp; Export</em> and tap <em>Default sound</em>, which clears it together with the instrument's other settings. Deleting the app also removes it.</p>
