+            <p><strong>Audio Input:</strong> <strong>Up to version 10.79.491 Echoelmusic does not use the microphone</strong>; the earlier audio-input path was removed on 2026-09-12. <strong>From the next version on, the microphone is used for one thing only: recording onto an audio track you armed yourself.</strong> iOS asks for permission when you arm such a track. Recording runs only between your tap on Record and Stop (or the end of the piece). The recording is saved as a file in the app&rsquo;s own media library on your device, so it is included in an iCloud or encrypted local device backup of your phone; it is never uploaded, analyzed by a server, or shared by the app. You can delete it like any other file in the library, and you can revoke microphone access at any time in iOS Settings. There is no live monitoring, no voice processing and no recording in the background. Apart from that, the only sound the app records is its own output, at your request, for export.</p>
